<pdd-reason>Deliver the approved Personal Files user experience as a native Ubuntu Rust application.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-dependency>core_rust.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>appearance_rust.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-interface>{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"run","signature":"() -> i32"}]}}</pdd-interface>
Implement src/ui.rs with gtk-rs GTK 3 bindings, safe Rust, Rc/weak UI callbacks, and a single background directory-scanning worker. Browser::new builds an independently testable GTK application window from an optional start path and injected Preferences. Match the approved story; no web server or Python runtime.
<contract_rules>
R1 - Show an always-visible path entry and a compact toolbar. Enter navigates immediately; resolve relative input against current folder, support tilde and absolute paths. A file path opens its parent and selects that file. Hidden files are always shown. Keep the current view after an invalid/unreadable path, with a readable status error. Startup restores the last successful folder and falls back to Home if unavailable.
R2 - Include Home, existing Desktop/Downloads and Computer under Places; persistent explicit Favorites; automatic Recent (7) and Frequent (5). Every successful navigation updates visits, but refreshing or monitor updates do not. One click on any sidebar row navigates. Full-path tooltips disambiguate duplicate basenames.
R3 - Favorite current folder with a star button or Ctrl+D. Context menus on folders and sidebar rows support Add/Remove Favorite. Drag one or more local directories to the sidebar to favorite them. Expose text/uri-list on drags; accept only local directory URIs, never execute their text, never move/delete the source. Unavailable favorites remain removable.
R4 - A multi-select file list has exactly Name, Modified, Size sort columns near its top. Click a header to sort, click again to reverse, folders first. Show folder size as an em dash. Preserve selection on refresh where possible. Double-click/Enter navigates folders or opens files via Ubuntu's registered default application without shell invocation.
R5 - Toolbar Copy and Ctrl+C copy selection full paths or current folder if selection is empty. Context menu also offers Copy Full Path and Copy Shell-Quoted Path. Ctrl+Shift+C copies shell-quoted paths. Use the real desktop clipboard, including clipboard-manager storage. Preserve native text copying inside the path entry.
R6 - Back/forward, Alt+Left/Right, parent folder Alt+Up, Ctrl+L focus/select address, Ctrl+R/F5 refresh. The Appearance menu exposes skins, Automatic, validated local image picker/removal, shortcut help and Clear Visit History. Settings persist immediately. Use GdkPixbuf to validate user images; bad images must not replace a working selection.
R7 - Coalesce queued directory scans to latest navigation on one worker and ignore stale results. All GTK work stays on the main thread. A local folder monitor debounces changes to refresh the list without inflating visit counts. Support manual refresh where monitoring is unavailable. Closing a window cancels monitoring and stops its polling. Preferences and scan errors must be visible rather than terminate the app.
R8 - Ubuntu only. CLI accepts optional PATH, --help, and rejects extra arguments. No-display launch must fail with an actionable message. App ID io.monoclaw.PersonalFiles. No telemetry, network services, or destructive file operations.
</contract_rules>
Retain the ignored desktop_story acceptance test in this module: opt in explicitly with a real display/xvfb; use temporary folders/preferences and assert GTK signals, clipboard text, navigation, favorites, sorting, drag URI handling, appearance CSS, monitoring, stale-result rejection and fresh-window persistence. Tests must not alter real preferences or open user documents. Distinguish callback tests from physical pointer-driven drag testing.
